  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.6.7: new rules FR0108-FR0116 (boolean identity/idempotent literals, missing DU cases, else-if flattening, equality-chain to match, nested-if merges, pyramid-of-doom flip, guard-order note, rec-group extraction incl. head re-crowning). FR0039 equality-with-ASCII-literal becomes a quick fix, with culture-aware alternatives offered in editors; FR0031 gains a String.Concat alternative. Fixes that move code carry their doc comments along, and a comment-preservation guard holds back any fix that would eat one — in editors too. Per-rule numeric config parameters (FR0114 thresholds first), and a \"suppressions\" policy that can keep correctness findings visible past suppression comments (--honor-suppressions restores them in CI).",
